# Stack conventions

## Architecture

- Static site only: Jekyll builds Markdown + Liquid → `_site`
- Collections: `stories`, `updates`, `projects` (see `_config.yml`)
- CMS: Decap at `/admin` with `git-gateway` on `main`
- Hosting: Netlify builds from GitHub; do not assume GitHub Pages

## Content rules

- New public content must include front matter compatible with `admin/config.yml`
- Listings must exclude unpublished docs, e.g. `where_exp: "item", "item.published != false"`
- Defaults already set `published: true` — set `false` to hide
- Uploads go under `assets/uploads/`; reference as `/assets/uploads/...`

## File discipline

- Layouts in `_layouts/`; shared chrome only in `default.html`
- One stylesheet: `assets/style.css` (CSS variables in `:root`)
- Keep README accurate if workflow/hosting docs change
- Do not add `node_modules`, React, or a second CSS framework unless asked
